+ * for the same glass, with two deliberate deviations:
+ *   - 0x21 (inversion on) is kept as 0x20 (off), because TuyaOpen packs bit 1 = black while
+ *     the Waveshare driver packs bit 1 = white. Same optical result.
+ *   - CASET/RASET are omitted; the driver programs them from x_offset/y_offset each flush.
+ * Format is {1 + data_len, delay_ms, cmd, data...}, zero terminated.
+ * Note 0xB0 gets overwritten with height/4 by the driver, which is 0x64 here anyway. */
